-- title:
--   Local conjugacy of the commutant order to a maximal order
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ and $\bar r$ be distinct primes. Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ has all nonzero elements invertible exactly when $r\in v$ or $\bar r\in v$; let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of it which is an order (contains $1$, is multiplicatively closed, spans the algebra over $\mathbb Q$, finitely generated) and is maximal among orders containing it. Let $c,d<0$ be such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,c,d]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly for $v$ containing $r$, with $O$ a maximal order in it, and let $a_1,b_1<0$ give the analogous condition at $\bar r$ for $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$. Let $j:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\to M_2(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,c,d])$ be a $\mathbb Q$-algebra map whose values on $\Lambda$ have all entries in $O$, and $\tau:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,c,d])$ an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map whose image is exactly the set of matrices commuting with every $j(m)$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule consisting precisely of those $x$ with all entries of $\tau x$ in $O$, and $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order in $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$. Finally let $w$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ with $r\notin w$ and $\bar r\notin w$. Then there is a unit $u$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_w$ such that, for every $x$ in this algebra, $x$ lies in [`Submodule.localBox R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) — the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb Q_w$ — if and only if $x=u\,y\,u^{-1}$ for some $y$ in the corresponding subgroup [`Submodule.localBox Λ₁ w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) attached to $\Lambda_1$.
--
--   This is the local comparison, at a place where all three quaternion algebras in play split, between the order $R=\tau^{-1}(M_2(O))$ cut out by the commutant embedding and an arbitrary maximal order $\Lambda_1$: away from $r$ and $\bar r$ the two local orders are conjugate inside the completed algebra. It is the away-from-ramification input to [`QuaternionAlgebra.exists_units_forall_mem_localBox_iff_of_forall_iff_mem_range_of_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.exists_units_forall_mem_localBox_iff_of_forall_iff_mem_range_of_isMaximalOrder), in the construction of the definite quaternion data used on the Čerednik–Drinfeld side.
